# `TZ`, stdio refill, and `ld-linux` RELRO faults

The issue was caused an accidental return value of the second `fread` to `/etc/localtime` in Docker env which is 0x3c, the syscall number for `exit` which is then mis-interpreted by the proxy loop as the signal for exit. Thus invoking the exit rountine in glibc with corrupt register values.

Fixed by reading the old system call number as rax will be updated after processing the system call.

# K8s application crash

There will be two types of the crash:

- The application hangs after entering the monitor. Likely due to a deadlock or something.
- The application returns with invalid register values and crashes.

